cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline or its results, please cite it as below, and cite the original data depositors listed in MANIFEST.tsv."
title: "arabidopsis-drem-osdr: a cell-type-weighted regulatory prior for DREM over NASA OSDR Arabidopsis pseudo-time-series"
abstract: >-
  A FAIR, reproducible pipeline that assembles cross-study pseudo-time-series from NASA
  Open Science Data Repository Arabidopsis thaliana studies and fits Dynamic Regulatory
  Events Miner (DREM 2.0.7) models over them, with a single-cell atlas acting on the
  model rather than on its annotation. iDREM can annotate finished nodes with cell-type
  data but does not use it when predicting the model; here cell-type context is written
  into the score column of DREM's TF-gene interaction input, so a transcription factor
  absent from the responding cell types is down-weighted before the search begins.
  Screening all 62 OSDR Arabidopsis studies yields a 10-timepoint gamma-irradiation
  series (10 min to 72 h, 108 timed samples, wild type and sog1-1) whose core is a
  re-assembly of one experiment deposited under three accessions, and a 3-timepoint
  spaceflight developmental series. The binding prior is built from the Arabidopsis
  DAP-seq cistrome, extended with SOG1 target edges called from the source study's own
  ChIP-seq because DAP-seq does not assay SOG1 -- without which no model could attribute
  any bifurcation to the master regulator of the response being modelled. Includes
  acquisition and analysis code, harmonised metadata, quality-control reports for every
  stage, a Crossref-verified bibliography, and a manuscript built to PDF and Word from
  one LaTeX source.
type: software
